 are reproducible across the generating environment and the 3.11/3.12/3.13 CI cells.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/config.py:25, certs.py:27,44, identity.py:21 all pass `formatter_class=argparse.HelpFormatter` (stdlib default), NOT the fixed-width RebarHelpFormatter","src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py:8,25,54 — RebarHelpFormatter exists precisely because stdlib HelpFormatter width is COLUMNS/terminal-dependent and non-reproducible","scripts/gen_cli_help.py render_route (line 85-89) formats help with no width/COLUMNS pin; _determinism_failures (line 131-134) only re-renders in the same process/env, so it cannot detect cross-environment width variance","Plan moves only `_unwrap_usage`/`_collapse_metavars`, which normalize usage-line wrapping and metavar repetition — not the wrapping of long description/option help (e.g. config validate's multi-sentence description, identity `--mapping` help)"],"finding":"The newly help-backed intercept parser factories build their parsers with the stdlib `argparse.HelpFormatter` (width from `shutil.get_terminal_size()`/`COLUMNS`), but `gen_cli_help.py` pins no width/COLUMNS, so the committed per-route intercept artifacts are terminal-width-dependent and the drift gate can pass in CI (piped stdout falls back to 80) yet fail after a developer regenerates in a non-80 terminal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f35f97d8337178085","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullets: 'Generate one committed artifact for each newly help-backed route'; 'Move `_unwrap_usage` and `_collapse_metavars`…'; 'The Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 CI cells must pass the help drift check against the same committed bytes.'","norm_id":"n661e85c357359c4f","priority":0.7,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A developer runs `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py` in a 120-column terminal, commits the intercept artifacts; CI (piped stdout, width 80) runs `--check` and reports every wrap-prone intercept artifact stale","config validate / identity intercept help lines wrap at a column that differs between the generating environment and the 3.11/3.12/3.13 CI cells"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In gen_cli_help.py's render path, force the fixed 80-column width for intercept routes (either construct the parser with RebarHelpFormatter, or set the environment/formatter width to _FIXED_WIDTH before format_help) so long-help wrapping is version- and terminal-independent, matching the existing core-command artifacts.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["46 file-impact entries (> 30)"],"finding":"Oversize signals suggest this unit may be too large for one session.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb59727dfac76fbbf","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"nd8e22e5830cb74a